+### Groups and memberships
+
+Groups organize the inbox; staff can still work on **all** tickets in their account. Staff can read the following resources; only admins can change them.
+
+| Method and path | Body / result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /groups`, `GET /groups/:id` | Page of `groups` in ID order, or one `group`. |
+| `POST /groups`, `PATCH /groups/:id` | `{"group":{"name":"Billing"}}` → created (`201`) or renamed `group`. Names are unique within the account, ignoring case. |
+| `DELETE /groups/:id` | `204`. Removes its memberships and clears both the group and assignee on its tickets. |
+| `GET /group_memberships`, `GET /group_memberships/:id` | Page of `group_memberships` in ID order, or one `group_membership`. The list accepts `group_id` and `user_id` filters together or separately. |
+| `POST /group_memberships` | `{"group_membership":{"group_id":20,"user_id":12,"default":true}}` → `201` with `group_membership`. `default` is optional. |
+| `PUT /group_memberships/:id/make_default` | Selects this membership as its user's default and returns `group_membership`. |
+| `DELETE /group_memberships/:id` | `204`. Clears this user's assignments in this group only, leaving those tickets grouped. |
+
+A staff member's first membership is always their default. Selecting another default replaces it. Removing the default promotes the remaining membership with the lowest ID, if any. Suspension clears the staff member's ticket assignments but keeps their memberships and default.
+
+On `PATCH /tickets/:id`, an assignee must belong to the selected group. Assigning someone on an ungrouped ticket uses their default group, or leaves the ticket ungrouped if they have no memberships. Moving a ticket without specifying an assignee keeps its current assignee only if they belong to the new group. `assignee_id: null` leaves the group unchanged; `group_id: null` clears both fields. These changes, like priority, are internal and are not visible on `/requests`.
